If all we can come up with is that an "Extropian relationship" is one
which is in accord with Extropian Principles, we haven't accomplished
anything interesting! It seems that there is a lot of definition-hunting
that goes on on this list. This thread and the one on "Children As Property"
seem to fall into this category. It seems as though Extropianism threatens
to become a religion. We are tempted to avoid the pain of making difficult
decisions by defining the problem away. Examples:

    1. Abortion is murder.
    2. Children are property.
    3. Imprisonment is deterrence.

I strive to attain a high level of autonomy in which I admit that some
decions are tough, decide freely anyway, and accept full responsibility for
these decisions. I never want to be an extropian zealot or ideologue who
